Analysis: QEMU is running successfully with VNC on port 5901 and QMP on port 4444. The monitor socket is at /tmp/qemu-monitor.sock. Now I need to set up the web interface with noVNC and nginx.
Plan: 1. Start websockify to proxy WebSocket connections from a local port to VNC port 5901
2. Configure nginx to serve noVNC static files on port 80 and proxy WebSocket connections to websockify
3. Start nginx
4. Test QMP connection to verify programmatic keyboard input works
[tool_use bash_command] websockify --daemon --web /usr/share/novnc 6080 localhost:5901

[tool_use bash_command] cat > /etc/nginx/sites-available/default << 'EOF'
server {
    listen 80 default_server;
    listen [::]:80 default_server;

    root /usr/share/novnc;
    index vnc.html vnc_auto.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }

    location /websockify {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:6080;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400;
    }
}
EOF

[tool_use bash_command] nginx -t && service nginx restart

[tool_use bash_command] ss -tlnp | grep -E '80|6080'

