Analysis: The nginx.conf has a server block on port 80 that proxies to 8080, which is conflicting with the sites-enabled config. I need to update nginx.conf directly to proxy to websockify on port 6080.
Plan: 1. Update nginx.conf to proxy to websockify (6080) instead of 8080
2. Remove the sites-enabled config to avoid conflicts
3. Restart nginx
4. Test the web interface
[tool_use bash_command] cat > /etc/nginx/nginx.conf << 'EOF'
user  root;
worker_processes  1;

events {
